{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba skills/mission/SKILL.md | sed -n '245,285p'\"","aggregated_output":"   245\t\n   246\t#### Mandatory Closing Tasks\n   247\t\n   248\tEvery mission's tasks.md MUST include these closing tasks after all feature tasks:\n   249\t\n   250\t1. **Smoke test (mandatory).** Write or update one end-to-end test that runs the project's primary user flow against real dependencies. No project-internal mocks. Place it where the project's standard test command runs it. If the mission produces no runnable user flow, note that in the handoff.\n   251\t\n   252\t2. **Cleanup task (mandatory).** Remove unused dependencies, dead code, leftover scaffolding, temporary artifacts, and any backwards-compatibility shims. Workers sometimes leave debris that per-task validation does not catch. This task cleans up the codebase before the shape re-check so the re-check does not flag soon-to-be-deleted surface area.\n   253\t\n   254\t3. **Module shape re-check (mandatory for missions with 5+ feature tasks; optional otherwise).** Re-read design.md's module descriptions. For each module, compare the description to what the code actually exposes -- in whatever form is natural for the project (public functions, React props, HTTP endpoints, CLI flags, exported types, data schemas, message topics, job parameters, config keys, whatever contract callers actually depend on). If reality has drifted meaningfully from the description, either update design.md to match (deliberate change) or refactor the code back (unintended drift). \"Meaningful drift\" means: any public surface item added, removed, or renamed that is not reflected in design.md; any change to the vocabulary or contract callers depend on; or a cumulative widening where a module that was described as having N operations now has noticeably more. Temporary shims and internal helpers do not count. For small missions (under 5 feature tasks) a one-line \"no drift observed\" note in the handoff is sufficient -- this step exists to catch cumulative drift across many tasks, which rarely occurs in short missions. This catches drift that per-task scrutiny cannot see.\n   255\t\n   256\t   Write the findings to `mission/validations/module-shape-audit.md` -- a short free-form note listing each module, whether drift was found, and what was done about it (\"no drift,\" \"design.md updated,\" or \"refactored\"). No required format; the file exists as a record that the check happened.\n   257\t\n   258\t4. **CLAUDE.md + ARCH.md generation (mandatory).** If the project root does not have a CLAUDE.md, create one from [templates/claude-md.md](templates/claude-md.md) using the actual built codebase (real commands, real repo structure, real conventions). If a CLAUDE.md already exists, do not modify it. Similarly, if no ARCH.md exists, create one from design.md's architecture decisions as a living document. If ARCH.md already exists, do not modify it.\n   259\t\n   260\t5. **Documentation task (mandatory).** Write or update documentation for what was built. The orchestrator recommends the documentation scope based on what the feature tasks produce -- this varies by mission type. Not every mission needs install instructions, architecture diagrams, or API docs. Use terms from `UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md` consistently. Any commands shown in docs must be executed against the built artifacts and the actual output pasted -- don't show output that wasn't produced. If unsure what documentation is needed, ask the human during this review.\n   261\t\n   262\t6. **CI configuration task (optional).** Add or update CI/CD pipeline configuration. The orchestrator recommends whether to include this based on the change scope. The human decides during this review.\n   263\t\n   264\tIf the design (Phase 4.3) identified refactoring needed for existing code, those tasks go before the feature tasks in tasks.md.\n   265\t\n   266\tPresent the full task list (including closing tasks) to the human with a recommendation. If approved, proceed to Phase 4a.\n   267\t\n   268\tAfter all artifacts are reviewed and approved, update the plan with the actual artifact paths.\n   269\t\n   270\t**Gate -- proceed when:**\n   271\t- [ ] proposal.md human-approved\n   272\t- [ ] All specs/<capability>/spec.md files human-approved\n   273\t- [ ] design.md human-approved\n   274\t- [ ] tasks.md (with closing tasks) human-approved\n   275\t- [ ] Plan updated with actual artifact paths\n   276\t\n   277\t---\n   278\t\n   279\t## Phase 4a: Spec Coverage Audit\n   280\t\n   281\t> **Rules:** 5\n   282\t> **Goal:** Verify every PRD requirement maps to at least one task before writing the contract.\n   283\t> **Inputs:** PRD (read from GitHub issue URL in plan), specs/, tasks.md\n   284\t> **Outputs:** coverage-audit.md, updated specs/tasks if gaps found\n   285\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
