{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba skills/mission/templates/claude-md.md | sed -n '1,80p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t| Include | Exclude |\n     2\t|---------|---------|\n     3\t| Commands Claude cannot guess | Anything Claude can infer from code |\n     4\t| Code style rules that differ from defaults | Standard language conventions |\n     5\t| Testing instructions and preferred runners | Detailed API docs (link instead) |\n     6\t| Architectural decisions specific to project | File-by-file codebase descriptions |\n     7\t| Dev environment quirks (required env vars) | Long explanations or tutorials |\n     8\t| Common gotchas or non-obvious behaviors | Self-evident practices |\n     9\t\n    10\tFor each line, ask: would removing this cause Claude to make mistakes? If not, cut it.\n    11\t\n    12\t## Template\n    13\t\n    14\t```markdown\n    15\t# <project-name>\n    16\t\n    17\t## Purpose\n    18\t<One paragraph: what this project does and who it's for>\n    19\t\n    20\t## Rules\n    21\t<Specific, actionable coding rules. Include \"update ARCH.md when you change architecture.\" Only rules that differ from language defaults.>\n    22\t\n    23\t## Commands\n    24\t<build, test, lint, format commands. Only commands Claude cannot guess from build files.>\n    25\t\n    26\t## Repo Map\n    27\t<High-level: what lives where. One line per major directory or module. Not file-by-file.>\n    28\t\n    29\t## Testing\n    30\t<Framework, where tests go by change type, any special setup like serial execution or DB requirements.>\n    31\t\n    32\t## Environment\n    33\t<Required services, env vars, config files, dev setup quirks.>\n    34\t\n    35\t## Architecture\n    36\tSee @ARCH.md for architecture decisions.\n    37\t\n    38\t## Key Terms\n    39\tSee @UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md for domain terminology.\n    40\t```\n    41\t\n    42\t## Example\n    43\t\n    44\tAdapt section content to the project's language and framework. The example below is illustrative; match the density and specificity to your project.\n    45\t\n    46\t```markdown\n    47\t# Invoice Sync\n    48\t\n    49\t## Purpose\n    50\tSyncs customer invoices from the billing system into the accounting ledger for operations staff.\n    51\t\n    52\t## Rules\n    53\tKeep ledger writes idempotent. Put provider-specific code behind adapters. Update ARCH.md when you change architecture.\n    54\t\n    55\t## Commands\n    56\t`make test` runs unit and integration tests. `make lint` runs formatting and static checks.\n    57\t\n    58\t## Repo Map\n    59\t`cmd/` holds entrypoints. `core/` holds invoice and ledger rules. `adapters/` holds external service clients.\n    60\t\n    61\t## Testing\n    62\tUse unit tests for `core/` changes and integration tests for adapter behavior. Ledger integration tests require `LEDGER_TEST_URL`.\n    63\t\n    64\t## Environment\n    65\tCopy `.env.example` to `.env`. Local runs require billing and ledger sandbox credentials.\n    66\t\n    67\t## Architecture\n    68\tSee @ARCH.md for architecture decisions.\n    69\t\n    70\t## Key Terms\n    71\tSee @UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md for domain terminology.\n    72\t```\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
