{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba skills/mission/templates/worker-brief.md | sed -n '1,90p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Worker Brief: Task N - <name>\n     2\t\n     3\t## Your Task\n     4\t<task description from tasks.md, expanded with acceptance criteria>\n     5\t\n     6\t## Project Context\n     7\t<relevant excerpt from proposal.md -- what is being built and why>\n     8\t\n     9\t## Architecture\n    10\t<relevant excerpt from design.md -- how this task fits into the system>\n    11\t\n    12\t## Key Terms (from UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md)\n    13\t<any domain terms the worker needs to understand>\n    14\t\n    15\t## What Previous Tasks Built\n    16\t<For task 1, this section is empty: \"This is the first task. No prior code has been committed for this mission.\"\n    17\t\n    18\tFor task 2+, include a codebase delta summary generated from `git diff` after each previous task passed validation. List ONLY observable facts about the code -- never include worker reasoning, handoff content, or concerns.\n    19\t\n    20\tFor each completed task, include:\n    21\t- Files created or modified (paths only)\n    22\t- Public function/endpoint signatures added (name, params, return type)\n    23\t- Key type definitions or interfaces introduced\n    24\t- Patterns used (e.g., \"repository pattern via src/repositories/userRepo.ts\")\n    25\t\n    26\tExample:\n    27\t### Task 1: User service\n    28\t- Created: src/services/users.ts, src/models/user.ts, src/repositories/userRepo.ts\n    29\t- Endpoints: POST /api/users (body: {email: string, name: string}) → 201 {id, email, name}\n    30\t- Types: User {id: string, email: string, name: string, createdAt: Date}\n    31\t- Pattern: repository pattern via src/repositories/userRepo.ts\n    32\t\n    33\t### Task 2: Auth middleware\n    34\t- Created: src/middleware/requireAuth.ts, src/services/auth.ts\n    35\t- Exports: requireAuth (Express middleware, attaches req.user: User)\n    36\t- Endpoints: POST /api/auth/login (body: {email, password}) → 200 {token: string}\n    37\t>\n    38\t\n    39\t## Downstream Consumers\n    40\t<Which later tasks in tasks.md will call this code? For each, name one minimum integration test that proves the call path works. Leave empty if no later task consumes this one.>\n    41\t\n    42\t## Procedures\n    43\t- Use `/tdd` to implement this task\n    44\t- Commit all changes (code + tests) in a single commit with message: \"[task-N] <description>\"\n    45\t- Write your handoff report to openspec/changes/<change-name>/mission/handoffs/task-N.md\n    46\t\n    47\t## Handoff Report Format\n    48\t- Task: Task N - <name>\n    49\t- Commit SHA: <the full SHA>\n    50\t- Approach: <brief explanation of what you did and why>\n    51\t- Commands run: <any commands and their exit codes>\n    52\t- Concerns: <anything you're uncertain about>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
