{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba skills/mission/SKILL.md | sed -n '470,545p'\"","aggregated_output":"   470\t- [ ] briefs/, handoffs/, validations/, issues/, logs/ subdirectories created\n   471\t\n   472\t---\n   473\t\n   474\t## Phase 7: Launch Confirmation\n   475\t\n   476\t> **Rules:** 5\n   477\t> **Goal:** Get human confirmation before starting the build.\n   478\t> **Inputs:** tasks.md, contract.md, coverage-audit.md, config.yaml\n   479\t> **Outputs:** Human approval, progress.md updated, plan status = BUILDING\n   480\t\n   481\tEnsure a feature branch. If `git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD` equals `gh api repos/{owner}/{repo} --jq .default_branch` (abort Phase 7 if that gh call fails -- it means no GitHub remote or bad auth), run `git checkout -b mission/<change-name>` -- if that branch already exists, use `mission/<change-name>-$(date -u +%Y%m%d%H%M%S)`. Log the checkout to progress.md.\n   482\t\n   483\tShow the user a summary dashboard:\n   484\t1. **Mission overview** -- change name, total tasks (feature + closing), total contract assertions\n   485\t2. **Coverage audit result** -- number of PRD requirements covered, any deferred/skipped items\n   486\t3. **Engine config** -- which engine runs each role (from config.yaml)\n   487\t\n   488\tAsk: \"Everything has been reviewed. Ready to start the build?\"\n   489\t\n   490\t- If yes: append `<timestamp> -- Plan approved. <N> tasks, <M> assertions in contract.` to progress.md. Update plan status to BUILDING. Post a comment on the PRD issue: `gh issue comment <number> --body \"Mission dispatched. <N> tasks, <M> assertions. Draft PR will link back on completion.\"` Proceed to Phase 8.\n   491\t- If the human wants to revisit something: loop back to the specific phase they name. Do not re-review everything.\n   492\t\n   493\t**Gate -- proceed when:**\n   494\t- [ ] Human confirms \"ready to start the build\"\n   495\t- [ ] progress.md updated with approval timestamp and task/assertion counts\n   496\t- [ ] Plan status = BUILDING\n   497\t\n   498\t---\n   499\t\n   500\t## Phase 8: Build Loop\n   501\t\n   502\t> **Rules:** 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 9\n   503\t> **Goal:** Build all tasks with per-task validation.\n   504\t> **Inputs:** tasks.md, contract.md, design.md, proposal.md, config.yaml, UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md\n   505\t> **Outputs:** Committed code per task, validation reports in mission/validations/. Codebase deltas are internal (populate subsequent task briefs within this phase).\n   506\t\n   507\tFor each unchecked task (`- [ ]`) in tasks.md, run Steps 1-7. Process tasks in order, one at a time (serial execution). Skip tasks marked `- [~]` (skipped) and `- [x]` (complete).\n   508\t\n   509\t### Step 1: Assemble Brief\n   510\t\n   511\tWrite a brief to `mission/briefs/task-N.md`.\n   512\t\n   513\t#### Brief Template\n   514\t\n   515\tRead [templates/worker-brief.md](templates/worker-brief.md).\n   516\t\n   517\t**The brief NEVER contains contract.md content.** \n   518\t\n   519\t### Step 2: Dispatch Worker\n   520\t\n   521\tRead the engine from `mission/config.yaml`.\n   522\t\n   523\t#### If engine is `codex`:\n   524\t\n   525\tBefore dispatching, run `git rev-parse HEAD` and store the result as `PRE_TASK_SHA`. This value is used in Step 7 to generate the codebase delta — store it somewhere you can reference after the background worker returns (e.g. in the plan file or a local variable).\n   526\t\n   527\tUse the Bash tool with `run_in_background: true` to run the worker. Use this exact bash script:\n   528\t\n   529\t```bash\n   530\tBRIEF_PATH=\"<absolute path to mission/briefs/task-N.md>\"\n   531\tHANDOFF_PATH=\"<absolute path to mission/handoffs/task-N.md>\"\n   532\tLOG_PATH=\"<absolute path to mission/logs/task-N-codex.log>\"\n   533\tPRE_TASK_SHA=$(git rev-parse HEAD)\n   534\t# Clean stale temp files and directories from previous workers to avoid filling /tmp\n   535\tfind /tmp -mindepth 1 -maxdepth 1 -user \"$(whoami)\" -mmin +30 -not -name \"claude-*\" \\( -type f -delete -o -type d -exec rm -rf {} + \\) 2>/dev/null\n   536\t\n   537\t# Dispatch via darkfactory-dispatch: process supervisor with timeout, heartbeat, and structured JSON result\n   538\tDISPATCH_RESULT=$(darkfactory-dispatch \\\n   539\t  --model gpt-5.5 \\\n   540\t  --effort high \\\n   541\t  --timeout 1800 \\\n   542\t  --sandbox workspace-write \\\n   543\t  --config 'sandbox_workspace_write.writable_roots=[\".git\"]' \\\n   544\t  --prompt-file \"$BRIEF_PATH\" \\\n   545\t  --output \"$HANDOFF_PATH\" \\\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
