{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba skills/mission/SKILL.md | sed -n '545,635p'\"","aggregated_output":"   545\t  --output \"$HANDOFF_PATH\" \\\n   546\t  --cwd \"$(pwd)\" \\\n   547\t  --log \"$LOG_PATH\" \\\n   548\t  --json 2>>\"$LOG_PATH\")\n   549\t\n   550\tif [ -z \"$DISPATCH_RESULT\" ]; then\n   551\t  echo \"TASK_FAILED: dispatcher crashed with no output. Log: $LOG_PATH\"\n   552\telse\n   553\t  DISPATCH_STATUS=$(echo \"$DISPATCH_RESULT\" | jq -r '.status')\n   554\t  DISPATCH_ERROR=$(echo \"$DISPATCH_RESULT\" | jq -r '.error.message // empty')\n   555\t\n   556\t  if [ \"$DISPATCH_STATUS\" = \"completed\" ] && [ -f \"$HANDOFF_PATH\" ]; then\n   557\t    echo \"TASK_COMPLETE: handoff written\"\n   558\t  else\n   559\t    echo \"TASK_FAILED: dispatch status $DISPATCH_STATUS${DISPATCH_ERROR:+; error: $DISPATCH_ERROR}; handoff $([ -f \"$HANDOFF_PATH\" ] && echo present || echo missing). Log: $LOG_PATH\"\n   560\t  fi\n   561\tfi\n   562\t```\n   563\t\n   564\tThe Bash tool returns a shell task ID immediately and notifies you when it completes. On completion, call BashOutput on that shell task ID to retrieve stdout. The only thing on stdout is the single final line -- either `TASK_COMPLETE` or `TASK_FAILED` -- because all codex output was redirected to `$LOG_PATH`.\n   565\t\n   566\t- `TASK_COMPLETE` -> proceed to Step 3\n   567\t- `TASK_FAILED` -> proceed to Step 3 (failure path). Read `$LOG_PATH` for failure context before asking the human.\n   568\t\n   569\t**Human visibility:** To watch dispatch progress live, run `tail -f <absolute path to mission/logs/task-N-codex.log>` in another terminal. The log contains both codex output and dispatcher events (heartbeats every 15 seconds, timeout warnings, tool activity). If the configured timeout is reached, the dispatcher kills the codex process automatically (SIGTERM at soft timeout, SIGKILL after grace period).\n   570\t\n   571\t#### If engine is `claude`:\n   572\t\n   573\tUse the Agent tool to spawn a subagent. Pass the full brief content as the prompt. Instruct the subagent to write its handoff to the same path (`mission/handoffs/task-N.md`).\n   574\t\n   575\t### Step 3: Handle Result\n   576\t\n   577\tRead the handoff file at `mission/handoffs/task-N.md`.\n   578\t\n   579\t- **TASK_COMPLETE** (handoff exists and contains a commit SHA): Extract the commit SHA. Log to progress.md: `<timestamp> -- Task N: worker completed. Commit: <SHA>`. Proceed to Step 4.\n   580\t- **TASK_FAILED** (handoff missing or no commit SHA):\n   581\t  1. If engine is `codex` and this is the first failure for this task: log to progress.md: `<timestamp> -- Task N: codex worker failed. Falling back to claude worker.` Append a line to `mission/fallbacks.log`: `task-N|<task-name>|<reason for failure>`. Then dispatch a claude worker (Opus 4.6, extended thinking high) using the existing \"If engine is `claude`\" dispatch path with the same brief. Wait for the result.\n   582\t     - If the claude fallback produces `TASK_COMPLETE`: log to progress.md: `<timestamp> -- Task N: claude fallback succeeded. Commit: <SHA>.` Proceed to Step 4.\n   583\t     - If the claude fallback also fails: fall through to the human escalation below.\n   584\t  2. Human escalation (reached when: engine is `claude`, engine is `codex` and both attempts failed, or any second failure): log to progress.md: `<timestamp> -- Task N: worker FAILED. <reason>.` Ask the human: retry, skip, or abort. If skip: mark the task as `- [~]` in tasks.md and log `<timestamp> -- Task N: SKIPPED by human.` to progress.md. The build loop ignores `- [~]` tasks.\n   585\t  3. On the next task, revert to the configured engine. This fallback is per-task only. Before starting the next task, re-read `engine` from `openspec/changes/<change-name>/mission/config.yaml` so the engine resets to the configured value after any Codex -> Claude fallback.\n   586\t\n   587\t### Step 4: Scrutiny Validation\n   588\t\n   589\tSpawn a Claude subagent (via the Agent tool) with this prompt:\n   590\t\n   591\t#### Scrutiny Validator Prompt\n   592\t\n   593\tRead [prompts/scrutiny-validator.md](prompts/scrutiny-validator.md) and use it as the subagent prompt. Fill in the commit SHA and contract assertions for this task. The prompt runs 11 checks: test presence, build, tests, lint, code review, module depth, code standards, simplify, security (if applicable), contract assertions, behavioral conformance.\n   594\t\n   595\tRead the validator's report from `mission/validations/task-N-scrutiny.md`.\n   596\t\n   597\t### Step 5: Handle Scrutiny Validation Result\n   598\t\n   599\t- **PASS**: Log to progress.md: `<timestamp> -- Task N: scrutiny validation PASSED.` Proceed to Step 6.\n   600\t- **FAIL**: Proceed to Step 5a (fix loop).\n   601\t\n   602\t### Step 5a: Fix Loop\n   603\t\n   604\tTrack the attempt number (starts at 1 for the initial worker, increments on each fix).\n   605\t\n   606\t1. **Write failure details** to `mission/issues/task-N-v<attempt>.md`:\n   607\t\n   608\t```markdown\n   609\t# Issue: Task N - <name> (Attempt <attempt>)\n   610\t\n   611\t## Failed Checks\n   612\t<list of failed checks from validator report>\n   613\t\n   614\t## Observed Symptoms\n   615\t<describe what went wrong in terms of behavior -- error messages, test failures, unexpected output. Do NOT copy contract assertion text here.>\n   616\t\n   617\t## Validator Recommendations\n   618\t<recommendations from validator>\n   619\t```\n   620\t\n   621\t2. **Circuit breaker check:** If attempt >= 3, stop the loop. Log to progress.md: `<timestamp> -- Task N: circuit breaker triggered after <attempt> attempts.` Update plan status to PAUSED. Ask the human: \"Task N has failed validation 3 times. Options: retry (allows one more attempt, counter continues from current value), skip (mark as skipped with `- [~]`, continue to next task), abort (stop the mission).\"\n   622\t\n   623\t   - **Retry:** Increment the attempt counter by 1 (e.g., attempt 3 becomes attempt 4). Allow one more fix attempt. If it fails again, the circuit breaker triggers again at the new count. Retry does NOT reset the counter.\n   624\t   - **Skip:** Mark the task as `- [~]` in tasks.md. Log to progress.md: `<timestamp> -- Task N: SKIPPED by human after <attempt> failed attempts.` Continue to the next unchecked task. The build loop ignores `- [~]` tasks (they are neither unchecked nor complete).\n   625\t   - **Abort:** Update plan status to PAUSED. Stop the build loop. Close the PRD issue with a reason: `gh issue close <PRD issue number> --reason \"not planned\" --comment \"Mission aborted at task N after <attempt> failed validation attempts.\"` Report to the human.\n   626\t\n   627\t3. **Diagnostic triage.** Spawn a lightweight Claude subagent to diagnose the failure. The subagent receives:\n   628\t   - The validator report (from `mission/validations/task-N-scrutiny.md` or `task-N-usertest.md` -- whichever triggered this fix loop entry)\n   629\t   - The worker's diff (`git show <commit-sha>`)\n   630\t\n   631\t   The subagent does NOT receive `contract.md`, `proposal.md`, or `design.md`. It describes what the code does wrong, not what the contract expected.\n   632\t\n   633\t   Subagent prompt: \"You are diagnosing a validation failure. Read the validator report and the code diff. For each failure, identify the probable root cause: which file and line, what the code does, and why that causes the observed symptom. Be specific -- name files, lines, variables, and values. Describe what the code does wrong, not what it should do. Write your triage to: `<path to mission/issues/task-N-v<attempt>-triage.md>`\"\n   634\t\n   635\t   The triage output is included in the fix brief (Step 4 below) as an additional \"Diagnostic Triage\" section. If the triage subagent fails or times out, skip it and proceed with the fix brief without it -- triage is helpful but not blocking.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
